Actually here in Miami,
and the police officer says

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.413
"Why you speeding? Why
you in such a hurry?"

00:10:41.413 --> 00:10:44.293
I'm like, "Dude I'm trying to
stay away from the crazies."

00:10:44.293 --> 00:10:47.935
Okay, if I can just get
ahead of everybody else

00:10:47.935 --> 00:10:51.984
I'm not distracted by
anybody but guys like you.

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:53.905
And your job is to stop me

00:10:53.905 --> 00:10:56.592
but the truth is, their job
it to stop me, distract me

00:10:56.592 --> 00:10:58.284
and cause me to turn around

00:10:58.284 --> 00:11:00.682
and stop my mission.

00:11:00.682 --> 00:11:02.861
See, so I got my ticket and moved on

00:11:02.861 --> 00:11:04.773
and went to the head of the pack again.

00:11:04.773 --> 00:11:05.697
See, this is what I'm telling you man.

00:11:05.697 --> 00:11:08.639
Look, if you want to not be bogged down

00:11:08.639 --> 00:11:10.708
by negative distractive people

00:11:10.708 --> 00:11:12.516
you need to take responsibility

00:11:12.516 --> 00:11:14.432
that you're slowing down enough

00:11:14.432 --> 00:11:17.845
to get caught up by this magnetic charge

00:11:17.845 --> 00:11:20.883
of distractive and negative people.

00:11:20.883 --> 00:11:22.546
Dude, you need to vibrate so fast

00:11:22.546 --> 00:11:25.401
that these people are distracting
other people, not you.

00:11:25.401 --> 00:11:26.882
Get way ahead of the crowd.

00:11:26.882 --> 00:11:30.221
Get so busy that nobody's
going to jack with you man

00:11:30.221 --> 00:11:31.909
because you're filling up your pipeline.

00:11:31.909 --> 00:11:33.244
You're full, you're busy

00:11:33.244 --> 00:11:36.124
and you don't have this
stuff sticking to you.

00:11:36.124 --> 00:11:38.903
Over and over, almost
every seminar I go to

00:11:38.903 --> 00:11:40.331
somebody will walk up to me and say

00:11:40.331 --> 00:11:42.138
"Dude, how do you handle burnout?"

00:11:42.138 --> 00:11:44.677
And my reply is fast and simple.

00:11:44.677 --> 00:11:46.908
"I don't believe in burnout."

00:11:46.908 --> 00:11:48.563
That's right, I don't believe in burnout.

00:11:48.563 --> 00:11:49.999
Now, I know if you're experiencing

00:11:49.999 --> 00:11:54.166
the exhaustion that is associated
with this idea of burnout

00:11:55.049 --> 00:11:56.712
that nobody can prove by the way.

00:11:56.712 --> 00:11:58.520
That this seems impossible to you

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.971
that burnout doesn't exist.

00:11:59.971 --> 00:12:01.409
But I'm telling you, listen to me.

00:12:01.409 --> 00:12:04.575
Burnout is not real, it's made up.

00:12:04.575 --> 00:12:06.583
Take a step back for just a second

00:12:06.583 --> 00:12:08.811
while I try to sell you on this idea.

00:12:08.811 --> 00:12:11.091
And try to remember a time

00:12:11.091 --> 00:12:12.874
when you were on fire.

00:12:12.874 --> 00:12:17.310
On fire, lit up, excited
about being an entrepreneur.

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.249
See that's gone right?

00:12:19.249 --> 00:12:21.099
"Yeah Grant, I'm burnt out.
That's what I'm telling you."

00:12:21.099 --> 00:12:21.932
No, no, no, no.

00:12:21.932 --> 00:12:24.863
Go back to the time when
you were lit up on fire.

00:12:24.863 --> 00:12:27.018
You couldn't sleep at night.

00:12:27.018 --> 00:12:28.954
You didn't need to eat okay?

00:12:28.954 --> 00:12:32.819
All you needed was the idea of a future

00:12:32.819 --> 00:12:34.707
you had for this dream, this idea

00:12:34.707 --> 00:12:35.769
this business, whatever.

00:12:35.769 --> 00:12:37.597
See at that time you were goal driven.

00:12:37.597 --> 00:12:39.864
The possibilities were enormous.

00:12:39.864 --> 00:12:40.928
They fed you.

00:12:40.928 --> 00:12:42.795
You were mission driven.

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:44.995
See, it's when the mission's missing.

00:12:44.995 --> 00:12:46.859
It's when the mission goes away

00:12:46.859 --> 00:12:49.122
that a person starts to
experience being tapped out.

00:12:49.122 --> 00:12:50.890
Or burned out.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:51.973
Or exhausted.

00:12:53.074 --> 00:12:54.612
At least this is my experience.

00:12:54.612 --> 00:12:57.299
Look, when I'm not tapped
fully into my future.

00:12:57.299 --> 00:12:59.360
My goals, the potential,
the possibilities.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.498
I don't care what the job is.

00:13:00.498 --> 00:13:02.709
Whether it was me when I
was working at McDonalds

00:13:02.709 --> 00:13:03.831
or the Country Club.

00:13:03.831 --> 00:13:07.604
I was working on a rig
down in the Gulf of Mexico

00:13:07.604 --> 00:13:10.340
or whether I was writing my first book.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:13.099
Look, when your goals aren't big enough.

00:13:13.099 --> 00:13:15.654
When you're no longer sold on your vision

00:13:15.654 --> 00:13:18.627
your purpose, your mission.

00:13:18.627 --> 00:13:21.781
The symptoms of losing interest,
what many call burn out.

00:13:21.781 --> 00:13:23.961
Burn outs are experienced.

00:13:23.961 --> 00:13:26.316
Any time you start reaching
for massive success

00:13:26.316 --> 00:13:27.572
the next thing.

00:13:27.572 --> 00:13:29.176
You start settling in.

00:13:29.176 --> 00:13:30.892
Getting comfortable.

00:13:30.892 --> 00:13:33.280
Listen, settle to settle.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.897
"Oh I just want to settle down."

00:13:35.897 --> 00:13:40.064
Dude, why don't you just decide
to hate your life every day?

00:13:41.491 --> 00:13:42.767
See, that's when you
start having problems.

00:13:42.767 --> 00:13:43.876
When you start settling.

00:13:43.876 --> 00:13:45.821
That's why comfort and complacency

00:13:45.821 --> 00:13:48.559
are the entrepreneur's worst enemy.

00:13:48.559 --> 00:13:49.862
In fact, I would tell you this.

00:13:49.862 --> 00:13:53.994
The comfort and complacency
are everybody's worst enemy.

00:13:53.994 --> 00:13:56.006
The only time I've ever
gotten in trouble in my life

00:13:56.006 --> 00:13:58.517
was when I was bored, complacent.

00:13:58.517 --> 00:13:59.904
When I was settling.

00:13:59.904 --> 00:14:01.552
Who wants average?

00:14:01.552 --> 00:14:03.435
Who wants average? Nobody wants it okay?

00:14:03.435 --> 00:14:05.682
Nobody, no matter where you're at in life

00:14:05.682 --> 00:14:07.604
you don't want average.

00:14:07.604 --> 00:14:09.884
But we're surrounded by
average people every day.

00:14:09.884 --> 00:14:11.683
Average ideas, average products.

00:14:11.683 --> 00:14:13.479
Average advertising.

00:14:13.479 --> 00:14:17.052
Only those that have given up on greatness

00:14:17.052 --> 00:14:19.141
would settle for average.

00:14:19.141 --> 00:14:20.744
Hey I want to talk to
you today about success.

00:14:20.744 --> 00:14:24.393
Success, duty, obligation, responsibility.

00:14:24.393 --> 00:14:26.252
If you approach it any other way

00:14:26.252 --> 00:14:27.407
which most people are.

00:14:27.407 --> 00:14:29.840
Most people think,
"Well I'll be successful

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.074
"If the economy works.

00:14:31.074 --> 00:14:33.575
"I'll be successful if something happens.

00:14:33.575 --> 00:14:35.910
"I'll be successful if I
win the lottery ticket."

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:36.988
Look, you're not going to be successful

00:14:36.988 --> 00:14:38.736
if you don't demand it.

00:14:38.736 --> 00:14:41.346
If you literally don't
stake a claim to it and say

00:14:41.346 --> 00:14:44.055
"This is mine, it's important."

00:14:44.055 --> 00:14:46.245
You're not going to
have it, I promise you.

00:14:46.245 --> 00:14:48.248
I know, I'm telling you from experience.

00:14:48.248 --> 00:14:50.410
I spent the first 25 years of my life

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.827
like a spectator.

00:14:52.894 --> 00:14:54.650
Watching other people get successful

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:56.601
and then wondering why I wasn't.

00:14:56.601 --> 00:14:59.183
Success is your duty.

00:14:59.183 --> 00:15:00.536
It is your responsibility.

00:15:00.536 --> 00:15:01.984
I'm sorry, your obligation

00:15:01.984 --> 00:15:04.010
and your responsibility.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.088
It's important.

00:15:05.088 --> 00:15:07.376
You know, I mean there's so many mistakes

00:15:07.376 --> 00:15:08.332
sales people make.

00:15:08.332 --> 00:15:10.674
I think you need to get
down to like, the main ones.

00:15:10.674 --> 00:15:12.987
But you're not selling the solution.

00:15:12.987 --> 00:15:15.931
Even before that though,
I would say Corrine.

00:15:15.931 --> 00:15:17.985
It's the biggest mistake,
people are not excited.

00:15:17.985 --> 00:15:19.112
They're not alive.

00:15:19.112 --> 00:15:21.985
They're not showing interest in the cycle

00:15:21.985 --> 00:15:23.018
and they lose interest.

00:15:23.018 --> 00:15:25.268
I was in Barcelona recently

00:15:26.502 --> 00:15:27.953
and I was looking at a watch

00:15:27.953 --> 00:15:30.203
and the cycle didn't close.

00:15:31.795 --> 00:15:32.700
I could have bought the watch.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.938
I was qualified to buy the watch.

00:15:33.938 --> 00:15:36.368
I'm the one that walked myself
in the shop on my vacation

00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:37.274
to look at the watch.

00:15:37.274 --> 00:15:39.211
I knew exactly the
watch I was looking for.

00:15:39.211 --> 00:15:40.545
And when I left my wife said

00:15:40.545 --> 00:15:43.250
"What could he have
done to close the sale?"

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.809
I said well he could have
kept life in the cycle.

00:15:46.809 --> 00:15:48.803
He could have kept the cycle open.

00:15:48.803 --> 00:15:51.257
So what I mean by that is
look, if you're not interested.

00:15:51.257 --> 00:15:54.021
If you don't believe
the cycle can be closed

00:15:54.021 --> 00:15:55.898
it will not close.

00:15:55.898 --> 00:15:58.156
So the number one mistake
I think sales people

00:15:58.156 --> 00:15:59.847
managers and the store makes

00:15:59.847 --> 00:16:03.557
is they assume a close
can't be had that day.

00:16:03.557 --> 00:16:05.112
I go into every cycle.

00:16:05.112 --> 00:16:08.687
Every sales cycle with every
prospect, every phone call.

00:16:08.687 --> 00:16:12.268
Every, no matter how complex the sale is

00:16:12.268 --> 00:16:13.346
or how simple it is

00:16:13.346 --> 00:16:17.309
with the belief that I can
sell that product that day.

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:19.310
This time, now.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.087
My message to you this week.

00:16:21.087 --> 00:16:24.477
Right now is not the time to stop.

00:16:24.477 --> 00:16:26.299
You can't stop.

00:16:26.299 --> 00:16:28.284
I wake up this morning and I'm like

00:16:28.284 --> 00:16:31.594
my God man what's going on,
what's happening to the world?

00:16:31.594 --> 00:16:34.584
Place is coming, you know
it's a scary place to live in.

00:16:34.584 --> 00:16:36.278
And I'm like, dude what are you doing?

00:16:36.278 --> 00:16:37.400
You're stopping right now.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.072
Now is not the time to stop or worry

00:16:39.072 --> 00:16:41.824
or back up or become apathetic.

00:16:41.824 --> 00:16:44.797
Now is the time to start again.

00:16:44.797 --> 00:16:46.711
That's right, again.

00:16:46.711 --> 00:16:48.250
It's like I've got to start over and over.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.089
I've got to continue every day like you do

00:16:51.089 --> 00:16:52.763
to improve yourself.

00:16:52.763 --> 00:16:55.973
Improve your skills, improve your game.

00:16:55.973 --> 00:16:57.800
Every day start over.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.711
Now is not the time to
start or back up or retreat

00:17:00.711 --> 00:17:02.747
or get lost in all the problems.

00:17:02.747 --> 00:17:04.910
Look, you've got to assume right now

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.287
that you can do way more, way more

00:17:07.287 --> 00:17:08.787
than you're doing.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.452
Ask yourself this question.

00:17:11.452 --> 00:17:13.583
I ask myself this probably
five times a week.

00:17:13.583 --> 00:17:15.334
Now, what is my potential?

00:17:15.334 --> 00:17:19.380
Is my potential greater than
what I'm delivering now?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:20.949
Regardless of what people think

00:17:20.949 --> 00:17:24.382
about my achievements or
my lack of achievements.

00:17:24.382 --> 00:17:26.081
Whatever the case is.

00:17:26.081 --> 00:17:27.557
I've been on both ends of this thing

00:17:27.557 --> 00:17:29.106
where people were disappointed with me

00:17:29.106 --> 00:17:30.625
early on in my life.

00:17:30.625 --> 00:17:32.471
And also today when people are like

00:17:32.471 --> 00:17:33.808
"Man, how do you get so much done?"

00:17:33.808 --> 00:17:36.637
Neither one of those should
be where you're living.

00:17:36.637 --> 00:17:39.610
It should be what is my potential?

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.527
What is your potential?

00:17:42.436 --> 00:17:44.228
Have you fulfilled that potential?

00:17:44.228 --> 00:17:46.930
Can you do more? Can
you make more contacts?

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.842
This is the model that we need to provide

00:17:48.842 --> 00:17:49.884
for one another.

00:17:49.884 --> 00:17:51.571
For our kids, for our parents

00:17:51.571 --> 00:17:52.921
for everyone in our community.

00:17:52.921 --> 00:17:56.189
Look, don't look for others to do this.

00:17:56.189 --> 00:17:57.561
They're not.

00:17:57.561 --> 00:17:58.559
Look around you

00:17:58.559 --> 00:18:00.737
and what you see is average everywhere.

00:18:00.737 --> 00:18:03.668
Average has become an epidemic.

00:18:03.668 --> 00:18:05.584
You don't have people living
up to their potential.

00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:07.508
You have people doing almost nothing.

00:18:07.508 --> 00:18:08.980
People retreating, back up.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.368
People that are lazy.

00:18:10.368 --> 00:18:12.621
People that have checked out.

00:18:12.621 --> 00:18:15.251
People that are waiting
for handouts and crumbs

00:18:15.251 --> 00:18:17.821
and think that will give them security.

00:18:17.821 --> 00:18:20.904
Look, now is the time to start again.

00:18:22.369 --> 00:18:25.148
Your security, your family's security.

00:18:25.148 --> 00:18:27.981
Your future is left in your hands.

00:18:28.906 --> 00:18:31.240
Your destiny is yours.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.195
Not someone else's.

00:18:32.195 --> 00:18:33.684
Nobody else can do for you.

00:18:33.684 --> 00:18:35.231
Nobody else can do it for me.

00:18:35.231 --> 00:18:36.645
It's your job and my time.

00:18:36.645 --> 00:18:39.024
Now is the time, now is the time to start.

00:18:39.024 --> 00:18:41.607
Now is the time to start again.

00:18:43.779 --> 00:18:45.092
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:18:45.092 --> 00:18:46.192
I hope you enjoyed.

00:18:46.192 --> 00:18:48.330
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:50.553
that you're going to immediately apply

00:18:50.553 --> 00:18:51.971
to your life or to your business.

00:18:51.971 --> 00:18:54.273
What was the most important
lesson that you learned?

00:18:54.273 --> 00:18:55.887
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:18:55.887 --> 00:18:57.225
I'm super curious to find out.

00:18:57.225 --> 00:18:59.714
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Simon Stanley.

00:18:59.714 --> 00:19:01.658
Simon, thank you do much
for picking up a copy

00:19:01.658 --> 00:19:03.049
of my book Your One Word.

00:19:03.049 --> 00:19:05.393
And making that awesome review
on your Youtube channel.

00:19:05.393 --> 00:19:07.166
I really, really appreciate the support

00:19:07.166 --> 00:19:08.806
and I'm glad you enjoyed the book.

00:19:08.806 --> 00:19:09.947
- What's good guys?

00:19:09.947 --> 00:19:11.011
Simon Stanley here

00:19:11.011 --> 00:19:13.193
and in this video, I'm
doing a video review

00:19:13.193 --> 00:19:16.557
of Your One Word, by Evan Carmichael.

00:19:16.557 --> 00:19:18.102
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:19:18.102 --> 00:19:20.119
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:19:20.119 --> 00:19:21.537
to believe in yourself

00:19:21.537 --> 00:19:23.233
and whatever your one word is.

00:19:23.233 --> 00:19:25.650
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:19:32.257 --> 00:19:34.716
- Well, when I was 16
I started using drugs

00:19:34.716 --> 00:19:37.633
and when I was 25 I was using drugs

00:19:38.637 --> 00:19:39.887
15 times a day.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:44.617
And I tried to quit for nine years.

00:19:44.617 --> 00:19:47.437
Every day for nine years man.

00:19:47.437 --> 00:19:50.081
So, then I went to a treatment center.

00:19:50.081 --> 00:19:52.957
Because my mom's like, "Hey
don't even come around."

00:19:52.957 --> 00:19:54.203
Everybody gave up on me.

00:19:54.203 --> 00:19:56.057
Like everybody, this isn't some kind

00:19:56.057 --> 00:19:57.431
of pulling hearts story.

00:19:57.431 --> 00:20:00.442
This is like, dude people hated me man.

00:20:00.442 --> 00:20:01.887
Okay, and the worst part of it

00:20:01.887 --> 00:20:03.054
is I hated me.

00:20:04.563 --> 00:20:05.876
So, it wasn't that.

00:20:05.876 --> 00:20:08.412
I was broke, I didn't
have a job, all of that.

00:20:08.412 --> 00:20:11.390
All the bad stuff but
the feeling that I had

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.223
about myself you know?

00:20:14.563 --> 00:20:15.480
Was just awful.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.924
So I went to the
treatment center you know?

00:20:17.924 --> 00:20:21.893
And got off the drugs, quit
using drugs for 25 days

00:20:21.893 --> 00:20:23.052
and they told me I had to leave

00:20:23.052 --> 00:20:26.349
