00:20:26.349 --> 00:20:27.941
What a scam that is.

00:20:27.941 --> 00:20:31.818
And the councilor dude, I
don't even remember his name

00:20:31.818 --> 00:20:33.872
but he told me on the way out, he's like

00:20:33.872 --> 00:20:35.320
"Hey man, let me tell you something."

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:36.851
Because see, I don't know if you've ever

00:20:36.851 --> 00:20:39.537
gone into one of these
12 step kind of deals

00:20:39.537 --> 00:20:41.359
but you go in and you do like

00:20:41.359 --> 00:20:44.339
this huge introspection on yourself

00:20:44.339 --> 00:20:46.276
and then you've got to
share with the group

00:20:46.276 --> 00:20:47.555
all your stuff.

00:20:47.555 --> 00:20:50.611
So I'm telling these guys
that I want to be rich

00:20:50.611 --> 00:20:52.389
and I think I'm James Bond

00:20:52.389 --> 00:20:55.971
and I'm the reincarnation
of James Bond and you know.

00:20:55.971 --> 00:20:57.937
(laughs)

00:20:57.937 --> 00:21:00.391
I'm going to write books dude,
I'm going to be famous man

00:21:00.391 --> 00:21:01.554
and people are going to see me

00:21:01.554 --> 00:21:02.890
and I'm going to do all this.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:04.524
Well, every time you do that over there

00:21:04.524 --> 00:21:05.987
they're like, "No, no dude.

00:21:05.987 --> 00:21:07.654
"Give up on the ego.

00:21:09.446 --> 00:21:11.526
"Give up on grandiosity.

00:21:11.526 --> 00:21:12.945
"You're not going to be rich.

00:21:12.945 --> 00:21:16.354
"If you just don't use
drugs one day at a time

00:21:16.354 --> 00:21:17.922
"Then you need to be happy."

00:21:17.922 --> 00:21:19.407
And the guy told me on
the way out of the place.

00:21:19.407 --> 00:21:22.170
He's like, "Look, if you
don't give up on all that

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.735
"You'll never make it."

00:21:24.735 --> 00:21:26.370
And I walked out of there and said

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.783
"Dude, I'm going to get rich.

00:21:28.783 --> 00:21:32.366
"I'm going to get rich,
I'm going to get famous."

00:21:33.334 --> 00:21:35.304
Because dude, I just couldn't live a life

00:21:35.304 --> 00:21:36.854
of just not doing drugs.

00:21:36.854 --> 00:21:39.773
Because I don't think
drugs was my problem.

00:21:39.773 --> 00:21:42.679
You know, it was just a
symptom of something else

00:21:42.679 --> 00:21:43.929
that went awry.

00:21:44.909 --> 00:21:47.039
And so, when I went back

00:21:47.039 --> 00:21:50.858
I took that addictive, that
you know 15 times a day

00:21:50.858 --> 00:21:52.386
and not trying to use drugs dude.

00:21:52.386 --> 00:21:54.344
I took that energy

00:21:54.344 --> 00:21:56.024
and I threw it in work.

00:21:56.024 --> 00:21:58.841
And you know how I am at work
dude, I'm a maniac you know?

00:21:58.841 --> 00:21:59.924
So, I took it

00:22:01.226 --> 00:22:02.852
and I basically, people started telling me

00:22:02.852 --> 00:22:06.880
"You just replaced one addiction
with another addiction."

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:09.818
And I'm like, "Yeah,
that's exactly what I did."

00:22:09.818 --> 00:22:14.028
I replaced one addiction with another one.

00:22:14.028 --> 00:22:17.283
And now I get addicted to
the good things in my life.

00:22:17.283 --> 00:22:20.777
The negativity is just negative.

00:22:20.777 --> 00:22:23.097
And there's no money in
it, there's no future

00:22:23.097 --> 00:22:24.151
in being negative.

00:22:24.151 --> 00:22:26.232
Where's the solution you know?

00:22:26.232 --> 00:22:28.319
"I can't do that, we can't do that.

00:22:28.319 --> 00:22:30.085
"That can't happen, this is wrong.

00:22:30.085 --> 00:22:32.554
"That's wrong, oh my
gosh taxes are too high.

00:22:32.554 --> 00:22:33.436
"Taxes are too."

00:22:33.436 --> 00:22:35.077
Dude, it's negative.

00:22:35.077 --> 00:22:36.477
It is negative.

00:22:36.477 --> 00:22:37.727
It is negative!

00:22:38.631 --> 00:22:41.257
Look, there's so much
abundance of negativity.

00:22:41.257 --> 00:22:45.499
That by itself tells you
why there's no value in it.

00:22:45.499 --> 00:22:47.591
I hear a lot of people
talk about one purpose

00:22:47.591 --> 00:22:48.918
and one thing you know?

00:22:48.918 --> 00:22:51.668
One thing has never filled me up.

00:22:53.182 --> 00:22:56.417
Whether it was one friend,
one drug, whatever dude.

00:22:56.417 --> 00:22:57.725
One doesn't work for me.

00:22:57.725 --> 00:22:59.642
One wife is good, that's all I need.

00:22:59.642 --> 00:23:01.516
I love my kids, one family you know.

00:23:01.516 --> 00:23:04.488
But I've always needed something else.

00:23:04.488 --> 00:23:08.360
You know, I need something
else to fill me up you know?

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:11.232
And it was, I'm 35 years old

00:23:11.232 --> 00:23:12.767
and these people are
like, "Dude when are you

00:23:12.767 --> 00:23:13.995
"Ever going to be satisfied?"

00:23:13.995 --> 00:23:16.310
I heard that a lot.

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:18.195
When's enough enough?

00:23:18.195 --> 00:23:19.139
You know?

00:23:19.139 --> 00:23:21.103
Whey can't you just enjoy what you have?

00:23:21.103 --> 00:23:24.150
Like something was wrong with me.

00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:26.791
And I bought it, I bought those ideas.

00:23:26.791 --> 00:23:27.898
I talk about this in the book

00:23:27.898 --> 00:23:31.398
about feeding the beast and starving fear.

00:23:34.215 --> 00:23:36.777
And I kept hearing about this you know.

00:23:36.777 --> 00:23:38.332
"Well you're never going to be satisfied."

00:23:38.332 --> 00:23:40.418
"Nothing fills you up

00:23:40.418 --> 00:23:41.752
"And that's why you're so disappointed."

00:23:41.752 --> 00:23:43.038
And people would say things like

00:23:43.038 --> 00:23:45.122
"Don't have high expectations."

00:23:45.122 --> 00:23:46.640
You know, Sam Walton

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:49.922
said the only way to live a
life is with high expectations.

00:23:49.922 --> 00:23:52.968
The only way to achieve anything
is with high expectations.

00:23:52.968 --> 00:23:57.706
But something happened in
America between 1980 and 2000

00:23:57.706 --> 00:24:01.333
where everybody started
doing this introspection

00:24:01.333 --> 00:24:02.916
feel your feelings.

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:06.777
What's the chick's name
over at Steve Carles place?

00:24:06.777 --> 00:24:08.875
The coach over there?

00:24:08.875 --> 00:24:10.083
- [Evan] Terry?

00:24:10.083 --> 00:24:14.335
- No the one that says go
inside of, what was her name?

00:24:14.335 --> 00:24:17.366
And I used her one time and
I said dude I can't do this.

00:24:17.366 --> 00:24:19.949
Because it's just not who I am.

00:24:21.023 --> 00:24:24.710
Like, I've done so much introspection

00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:27.118
that I couldn't do anything.

00:24:27.118 --> 00:24:30.475
I had to come and mobilize my purposes.

00:24:30.475 --> 00:24:31.688
I mean, what's wrong with somebody

00:24:31.688 --> 00:24:34.271
that wants to do another thing?

00:24:35.259 --> 00:24:39.033
You know, look I am not
fueled up by one person.

00:24:39.033 --> 00:24:41.042
My wife cannot fill me up.

00:24:41.042 --> 00:24:43.955
Two kids can't make me feel full

00:24:43.955 --> 00:24:46.881
because I think if people are obsessed

00:24:46.881 --> 00:24:48.335
with a lot of purposes

00:24:48.335 --> 00:24:50.690
and that's why people are dissatisfied.

00:24:50.690 --> 00:24:52.867
And my goal is that this book

00:24:52.867 --> 00:24:55.351
gives people permission to be.

00:24:55.351 --> 00:24:57.501
To not be so introspective

00:24:57.501 --> 00:25:00.660
but to actually become
obsessed with dreams again.

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:02.777
With possibilities.

00:25:02.777 --> 00:25:06.249
With the idea that you could be a husband

00:25:06.249 --> 00:25:08.903
a father, a community leader

00:25:08.903 --> 00:25:11.998
a church leader, you could
actually talk about politics.

00:25:11.998 --> 00:25:13.588
You could get rich.

00:25:13.588 --> 00:25:14.770
You could write books.

00:25:14.770 --> 00:25:16.365
You could find time to do all that

00:25:16.365 --> 00:25:19.017
and not even worry about balance.

00:25:19.017 --> 00:25:22.202
Because the obsession of
each one of those things

00:25:22.202 --> 00:25:23.692
would actually fill you up

00:25:23.692 --> 00:25:27.275
to have a life that
was naturally balanced.

